---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../assets/portrait.jpg';
---
<!-- About -->
<section id="about">
    <div class="section-header fade-in">
        <h2>About</h2>
        <div class="divider"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="about-content">
        <div class="about-image fade-in-left">
            <Picture src={portrait} formats={['avif', 'webp']} widths={[400, 600, 800, 1000]} sizes="(max-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 48px), 386px" alt="Brice Perkins, owner of Perkins Production in Frederick, Maryland" loading="lazy" decoding="async" style="width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:center;display:block;" />
        </div>
        <div class="about-text fade-in-right">
            <h3>Why a photographer builds websites</h3>
            <p>I'm Brice. I live in Frederick, Maryland, and I've spent my working life behind a camera: weddings, portraits, film, walking through buildings with a 3D scanner.</p>
            <p>The websites grew out of that. I kept watching good photography get poured into templates that flattened it, so I started building the sites myself, and now that is most of what I do. I've built the home of the JFK 50 Mile, America's oldest ultramarathon, a summer track series that has brought families out for more than 25 years, and a golf league I play in myself.</p>
            <p>All of it came from one person telling another, which is the only way I have ever gotten work. So when you hire me, you get one person the whole way through: the one who designs it, writes the code, sets up the hosting, and shows up with a camera when your site needs pictures that are actually yours.</p>
            <div class="signature">Brice Perkins</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
